\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces One iteration of the real-time adaptive loop. A gaze sample is mirrored to both surfaces over the realtime channel; the participant surface, which alone knows the rendered layout, maps it to a token and returns an enriched observation; analysis projects observations into oculomotor events; a decision (built-in, external, or the researcher acting manually) yields at most one proposal, which in advisory mode waits for researcher approval; the intervention commits at a controlled boundary and the adapted text returns to both surfaces. Persistence checkpoints are written best-effort throughout.}}{5}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:loop}{{3}{5}{One iteration of the real-time adaptive loop. A gaze sample is mirrored to both surfaces over the realtime channel; the participant surface, which alone knows the rendered layout, maps it to a token and returns an enriched observation; analysis projects observations into oculomotor events; a decision (built-in, external, or the researcher acting manually) yields at most one proposal, which in advisory mode waits for researcher approval; the intervention commits at a controlled boundary and the adapted text returns to both surfaces. Persistence checkpoints are written best-effort throughout}{figure.caption.8}{}}
